 "meta": {
  "source": "Isopedia (Zheng & Sedlazeck, bioRxiv 2026) \u2014 read-level index of 1,007 public human long-read RNA-seq samples; queried and aggregated in the user's own public_isoform project at /data/mdl_data/hyu/projects/public_isoform/isopedia (table_wide2/)",
  "dataset_description": "821 samples passing depth >= 200,000 indexed reads, 536 ONT and 285 PacBio, 64 BioProjects, 36 standardised tissues",
  "how_quantified": "`isopedia isoform -g gencode.v49.gtf` returns per-GENCODE-transcript, per-sample supporting read counts (RC_FSM_JC = reads whose junction chain fully matches; RC_EM_ISM = partial reads assigned by EM). Transcripts sharing an intron chain are collapsed to one splice-pattern isoform taking max(RC_FSM_JC)+sum(RC_EM_ISM); usage = isoform reads / gene reads in that sample. A (sample, gene) is measured at >= 20 gene reads; the panel keeps genes measured in >= 2% of samples; catalog isoforms must reach usage >= 0.05 in >= 5% of measured samples, everything else is pooled into 'other'. Built by tools/isopedia_context_table.py in ~/IsoMap-RNAFM/isoform_usage_benchmark.",
