  "denominator": "all reads Isopedia assigned to the gene, i.e. every splice pattern it saw, including isoforms this app does not model and the pooled 'other' bin. Per gene and sample, catalog usage + other = 1; our app isoforms cover only part of that.",
  "caveats": [
   "long-read quantification, not ground truth: EM assignment of partial (ISM) reads, 3'/5' degradation and library chemistry all shift usage",
   "annotation is GENCODE v49; the app is built on Ensembl 116, so app-only transcript ids are joined by intron chain, and transcripts that share an intron chain share one measured value",
   "heterogeneous public samples (tumour, cell line, tissue; ONT and PacBio mixed), not a matched panel, so 'overall' is a mean over a convenience sample",
   "isoforms below 5% usage in 95% of samples are invisible (pooled into 'other')",
   "mean is over samples, so a gene's measured fractions sum to 1 only when 'other' is included"
  ],
